WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.008
[opening theme music playing]

01:46.731 --> 01:49.025
[music fades]

01:49.109 --> 01:56.074
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

01:59.244 --> 02:00.995
FOR THE INDEPENDENCE OF KOREA

02:03.706 --> 02:05.041
So two weeks from today…

02:05.625 --> 02:08.128
…a fundraiser rally
for all the Japanese frontline generals

02:08.211 --> 02:09.462
will be held at Bumingwan.

02:09.546 --> 02:10.839
After the bombing of Tokyo,

02:10.922 --> 02:13.341
the Japanese army
is struggling to stay afloat.

02:13.424 --> 02:15.927
They're deploying our own Joseon men
to the front lines.

02:16.010 --> 02:17.637
So this propaganda rally is

02:18.513 --> 02:20.223
to raise funds for their war efforts.

02:20.306 --> 02:22.225
All the emperor's men
will attend that event.

02:22.308 --> 02:24.811
Lt. Col. Minami, Lt. Gen. Seijiro,

02:24.894 --> 02:26.062
Maj. Gen. Junji,

02:26.855 --> 02:28.022
Police Chief Nishimura,

02:28.106 --> 02:30.275
and Commissioner Ishikawa
will be attending.

02:30.358 --> 02:32.694
All the big names in Gyeongseong
will be there.

02:34.320 --> 02:37.073
Representing our people
is the United Society of Joseon,

02:37.157 --> 02:39.242
along with the People's Livelihood Corps.

02:40.326 --> 02:41.786
This is our opportunity.

02:42.537 --> 02:44.080
Jun-taek, you must attend that event.

02:47.959 --> 02:50.837
[man] So the leaders
of the Japanese occupation forces

02:50.920 --> 02:55.133
and the heads of the pro-Japanese traitors
will all be there, assembled in one place.

02:56.718 --> 02:58.887
It's an incredibly rare chance for us.

02:58.970 --> 03:03.057
We've still got all that dynamite we stole
when we planned the railway attack.

03:03.141 --> 03:04.350
Got about 20 kilograms.

03:05.435 --> 03:08.521
We had to abort the plan when Comrade Jung
ended up getting arrested,

03:08.605 --> 03:11.858
but, um, the dynamite
is still in our possession.

03:12.859 --> 03:15.778
We can't get caught.
This strike must happen no matter what.

03:17.071 --> 03:18.823
Comrade Kwon, don't you worry.

03:18.907 --> 03:20.658
I am the only one here
who knows where it is.

03:22.035 --> 03:23.536
I know where it's hidden.

03:31.294 --> 03:32.837
- [door opens]
- [man 1] Everyone, run!

03:34.172 --> 03:36.674
[unsettling music playing]

03:36.758 --> 03:38.468
[grunting, groaning]

03:39.219 --> 03:40.261
[man 2] Get out of here!

03:41.721 --> 03:43.723
[grunting, groaning]

03:45.433 --> 03:47.769
[officer shouting indistinctly]

03:50.563 --> 03:52.357
[breathing heavily]

03:52.440 --> 03:53.441
Comrade Kwon.

03:54.609 --> 03:55.818
[whispering]

03:57.987 --> 04:00.531
He was taken? On what charges?

04:01.366 --> 04:02.909
For spreading around rebel newspapers.

04:03.826 --> 04:06.829
Something's weird though. I was told
he wasn't put inside a normal prison.

04:06.913 --> 04:08.039
Where, then?

04:08.122 --> 04:09.707
He was taken over to Ongseong Hospital.

04:10.458 --> 04:11.459
[exhales]

04:13.628 --> 04:15.296
[unsettling music playing]

04:26.933 --> 04:27.934
[prisoner grunts]

04:29.560 --> 04:31.020
What? [pants]

04:33.022 --> 04:34.315
Are they leaving us here?

04:36.693 --> 04:41.614
LONG LIVE THE EMPEROR
DEVOTE ALL TO WAR

04:46.119 --> 04:48.121
[ominous music playing]

04:54.377 --> 04:55.461
Comrade Lee In-hyeok?

04:55.545 --> 04:56.879
[man 1] Who are you? Hey.

04:57.505 --> 04:59.966
- [man 2] Wait, are you from Joseon?
- [Jun-taek] Excuse me.

05:00.049 --> 05:02.010
[man 2] Hey, hey. Over here!

05:04.595 --> 05:06.389
- [door clanks]
- [woman 1] Please help us, sir.

05:06.472 --> 05:08.141
Please help us get out of here now.

05:09.434 --> 05:12.270
- Do you know who Comrade Lee In-hyeok is?
- I need your help, sir. Listen.

05:12.353 --> 05:14.188
I have two little kids at home, waiting.

05:14.272 --> 05:17.150
Hmm? Please, sir, I really need
to feed my kids. Can you help me?

05:17.233 --> 05:18.484
[woman 1 sobs]

05:18.568 --> 05:22.238
Please help me get back home!
Please, sir! Huh?

05:22.322 --> 05:25.700
I'm sorry, ma'am.
I'm on a more urgent mission right now.

05:25.783 --> 05:27.785
No, no. No, sir. Help me.

05:27.869 --> 05:29.495
[man 3] Over here! We're over here!

05:29.579 --> 05:31.289
- Over here! Here!
- Sir, help us, please.

05:31.372 --> 05:32.498
[woman 1 whimpers]

05:32.582 --> 05:34.584
- I'm very sorry.
- [woman 1] Sir, please! No.

05:35.293 --> 05:36.794
[woman 2] Please help me, sir!

05:37.587 --> 05:38.963
Comrade Kwon!

05:39.672 --> 05:41.341
Thank you for coming for us.

05:42.050 --> 05:45.261
Okay now. Help us.
Hurry and get us out of here.

05:47.638 --> 05:49.432
I don't have time right now.
I'm in a bad spot.

05:49.515 --> 05:51.351
- Wait, what are you saying?
- [distant clatter]

05:51.893 --> 05:54.312
Aren't you… aren't you here
to help us get out?

05:54.812 --> 05:57.231
I need you to tell me
where you hid the dynamite.

05:57.815 --> 06:00.276
We've got less than ten days
before the big rally.

06:00.360 --> 06:03.196
I don't know if we'll ever have
an opportunity like this again.

06:03.279 --> 06:06.657
You have to tell me, Comrade Lee.
Where'd you hide it? Where is it?

06:07.658 --> 06:08.868
I won't tell you.

06:10.453 --> 06:11.704
Get us both out of here first.

06:11.788 --> 06:12.830
[sighs]

06:13.956 --> 06:15.833
I can't afford to do that right now.

06:15.917 --> 06:18.544
Listen, first just tell me
where the dynamite is.

06:18.628 --> 06:19.545
[thumps chest]

06:19.629 --> 06:21.589
I promise as soon as I get out,
I'll be back.

06:22.090 --> 06:24.967
I will find a way to get you out of here.
I promise you that.

06:25.051 --> 06:27.512
- Get us out, or I won't tell you a thing.
- Tell me where it is!

06:27.595 --> 06:28.638
Listen to me!

06:29.180 --> 06:31.015
This place is a living hell, okay?

06:31.891 --> 06:33.768
This is not some ordinary prison!

06:33.851 --> 06:35.478
- [In-hyeok breathing heavily]
- [taps door]

06:36.604 --> 06:38.731
Comrade Kwon,
if you don't get us out of this place,

06:38.815 --> 06:40.400
then I won't tell you anything.

06:42.568 --> 06:44.695
I won't give you the dynamite.

06:44.779 --> 06:45.947
[rifles cock]

06:47.782 --> 06:48.866
Don't move a muscle.

06:49.617 --> 06:50.827
Put your hands above your head!

06:57.959 --> 06:59.001
[grunts]

07:00.878 --> 07:04.048
[heavy footsteps pounding]

07:08.553 --> 07:10.555
[tense music playing]

07:14.851 --> 07:16.853
[creature snarling]

07:22.859 --> 07:25.445
[roaring]

07:27.822 --> 07:30.199
- [breathing heavily]
- [creature roaring]

07:31.659 --> 07:33.369
- [creature roaring]
- [Tae-sang grunting]

07:34.745 --> 07:36.622
[panting, groaning]

07:38.666 --> 07:40.418
[music intensifies]

07:40.501 --> 07:41.669
[creature roaring]

07:50.553 --> 07:51.762
[rifle cocks]

07:52.847 --> 07:54.140
[creature groans]

08:01.689 --> 08:03.232
[creature growls]

08:06.986 --> 08:07.820
[rifle cocks]

08:09.280 --> 08:10.865
[creature growls]

08:13.910 --> 08:14.994
[low growl]

08:17.455 --> 08:18.623
[roars]

08:19.457 --> 08:21.292
[rifle clicking]

08:24.170 --> 08:25.546
[creature growls]

08:25.630 --> 08:27.298
- [rifle clicks]
- [creature growls]

08:27.381 --> 08:28.341
[breathing nervously]

08:30.009 --> 08:31.344
[creature roars]

08:34.096 --> 08:35.223
[creature roars ferociously]

08:39.393 --> 08:41.395
[creature growls]

08:47.235 --> 08:48.444
[roars ferociously]

08:48.528 --> 08:50.530
[tense music continues]

08:54.700 --> 08:56.369
[creature growls]

09:14.762 --> 09:15.680
[roars]

09:18.975 --> 09:20.601
[creature snarls]

09:37.952 --> 09:39.954
[roars ferociously]

09:44.584 --> 09:46.085
[roars ferociously]

09:50.715 --> 09:52.675
[growls]

09:55.678 --> 09:56.512
[grunts]

09:58.264 --> 09:59.932
- [Tae-sang grunts]
- [roars ferociously]

10:00.016 --> 10:01.309
[loud bang]

10:01.392 --> 10:03.185
[breathing heavily]

10:03.269 --> 10:04.395
[loud bang]

10:06.063 --> 10:07.189
[loud bang]

10:07.273 --> 10:09.191
- [both breathing heavily]
- [loud bang]

10:09.275 --> 10:11.902
- What was that? What was that monster?
- [creature growls]

10:11.986 --> 10:16.282
I have no idea what that thing even was.
However, I'm sure it was created in here.

10:16.365 --> 10:18.492
- [creature roars]
- [loud bang]

10:19.243 --> 10:20.369
[creature roars]

10:20.953 --> 10:22.079
[loud bang]

10:23.205 --> 10:24.498
[creature growls]

10:25.291 --> 10:26.375
[loud bang]

10:26.459 --> 10:27.960
[creature roars]

10:31.130 --> 10:32.298
[loud bang]

10:33.341 --> 10:34.967
[creature snarling]

10:35.051 --> 10:36.802
- [loud bang]
- [breathes nervously]

10:37.928 --> 10:39.055
- [loud bang]
- [grunts]

10:39.722 --> 10:41.682
[tense music continues]

10:41.766 --> 10:43.017
[loud bang]

10:45.227 --> 10:46.562
[loud bang]

10:51.025 --> 10:52.068
[loud bang]

10:54.403 --> 10:55.237
[loud bang]

10:57.907 --> 10:59.033
[creature snarls]

10:59.700 --> 11:00.826
[loud bang]

11:04.413 --> 11:06.415
- [breathing nervously]
- [loud bang]

11:10.961 --> 11:11.796
[loud bang]

11:11.879 --> 11:12.838
[creature growls]

11:15.675 --> 11:16.550
[roars]

11:18.177 --> 11:19.887
- [gunshot]
- [roars ferociously]

11:22.223 --> 11:23.516
[roars]

11:27.895 --> 11:29.397
[roars ferociously]

11:30.773 --> 11:33.234
Hurry. You have to find a way out of here.

11:33.317 --> 11:35.236
We can get to the central vent.

11:35.319 --> 11:37.196
It's behind this boiler room
we're in right now.

11:37.279 --> 11:38.280
Let's head over that way.

11:38.364 --> 11:40.282
[Chae-ok breathing heavily]

11:40.366 --> 11:42.284
- [rifle cocks]
- [tense music continues]

11:48.624 --> 11:49.792
[rifles cock]

11:53.129 --> 11:54.380
[creature growls]

11:55.715 --> 11:57.049
[roars]

11:59.885 --> 12:01.804
[roars]

12:04.932 --> 12:06.559
[roars ferociously]

12:08.394 --> 12:10.312
[breathing heavily]

12:11.731 --> 12:13.315
[creature roars]

12:16.402 --> 12:18.696
[roars ferociously]

12:19.780 --> 12:20.740
[roars]

12:24.785 --> 12:25.911
[creature growls]

12:31.542 --> 12:34.503
[snarling]

12:34.587 --> 12:36.505
[unsettling music playing]

12:41.343 --> 12:42.678
Drop your weapon.

12:45.014 --> 12:46.515
Did you not hear me?

12:47.266 --> 12:48.559
Knife on the floor.

12:53.481 --> 12:55.483
[breathes shakily]

13:04.366 --> 13:07.703
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN DENIAL AND TRUTH

13:07.787 --> 13:10.372
EPISODE 5
DESPERATION

13:11.207 --> 13:12.917
I told you to drop your knife!

13:17.338 --> 13:20.007
Chae-ok, listen.
Let's just do what he says for now.

13:20.966 --> 13:22.843
Why? He'll just kill both of us anyway.

13:22.927 --> 13:25.930
I'm just saying we're in a bad position
right now, and all bets are against us.

13:26.013 --> 13:28.140
It's always business for you, isn't it?

13:29.058 --> 13:30.392
You're always quick to give up.

13:30.476 --> 13:32.686
I'm quick to solve a bad situation.

13:32.770 --> 13:35.147
I'm built to handle crises well,
even the worst.

13:35.981 --> 13:37.900
Call it flexibility. [chuckles]

13:39.777 --> 13:41.779
Now isn't the time
to crack a joke, Tae-sang.

13:41.862 --> 13:44.323
At least we escaped
that horrible monster we ran into.

13:44.907 --> 13:45.991
Did we though?

13:47.535 --> 13:49.286
I question who the real monster is.

13:50.204 --> 13:51.789
This is your final warning.

13:52.456 --> 13:54.875
Put down the knife
and get on the ground now!

13:59.880 --> 14:01.423
[unsettling music playing]

14:03.050 --> 14:04.009
[chuckles softly]

14:10.224 --> 14:14.103
If we both go out like this,
then we will have lost to them.

14:14.186 --> 14:15.020
Surrender for now.

14:15.688 --> 14:17.731
There's no such thing as surrendering
in my book.

14:17.815 --> 14:20.359
Usually, it's the same for me,
but this is different.

14:20.442 --> 14:22.236
So just trust me. Drop the knife.

14:22.820 --> 14:26.073
I'm trying to keep us alive
so that we don't die here.

14:44.758 --> 14:45.968
[unsettling music subsides]

14:46.051 --> 14:47.553
[footsteps approaching]

14:51.181 --> 14:52.182
[soldier 1] Don't move!

14:52.850 --> 14:53.809
[Tae-sang grunts]

15:01.901 --> 15:03.861
[eerie music playing]

15:15.873 --> 15:17.583
We're still looking for the creature, sir.

15:18.375 --> 15:20.544
How many soldiers were killed
in the first platoon?

15:20.628 --> 15:22.504
All of them. There were no survivors.

15:40.564 --> 15:42.566
[distant clattering]

15:44.985 --> 15:46.236
Are you saying

15:47.613 --> 15:50.574
that it knows
how to operate the elevator on its own?

15:52.451 --> 15:54.453
How could you allow this to happen, huh?

15:54.954 --> 15:57.039
- And on your watch.
- My apologies, sir.

15:58.415 --> 16:01.794
We were all under attack.
We were ambushed so very suddenly, sir.

16:01.877 --> 16:04.296
So where is the creature right now?
Does anyone know?

16:04.380 --> 16:07.883
Don't worry, sir. The main elevator
has already been shut down,

16:07.967 --> 16:10.260
and the machine gun crews
are stationed at every route

16:10.344 --> 16:11.512
to the first-level basement.

16:11.595 --> 16:13.180
The situation is under control for now.

16:13.263 --> 16:15.516
I'm quite certain
this will all be over soon.

16:15.599 --> 16:18.602
Do you know what I hate
more than anything else, soldier?

16:19.103 --> 16:20.938
Problems that were completely avoidable.

16:22.439 --> 16:25.025
And what I hate even more is
when those avoidable problems

16:25.109 --> 16:26.235
take too long to get fixed.

16:26.944 --> 16:27.903
Forgive me, Director.

16:28.529 --> 16:31.407
Apologizing like a pathetic
and helpless schoolgirl

16:31.490 --> 16:34.159
instead of finding a way
to fix the problem.

16:34.243 --> 16:37.538
You're a complete failure in my eyes,
Mr. Soma.

16:41.625 --> 16:45.170
You, take care of it
before something even worse happens.

16:45.671 --> 16:46.505
Understood?

16:46.588 --> 16:47.631
[all] Yes, sir!

16:47.715 --> 16:48.966
[knocking at door]

16:51.176 --> 16:52.970
Director Ichiro, we captured a trespasser.

16:55.681 --> 16:57.850
- [unsettling music playing]
- [grunting]

17:03.147 --> 17:04.064
Look who it is.

17:04.648 --> 17:06.859
The young master of the Bugang Company.

17:07.526 --> 17:10.863
I've heard you're quite the troublemaker
and quite the headache.

17:10.946 --> 17:13.282
It seems like you're in
really big trouble now.

17:14.450 --> 17:16.910
Did your friend Jang Tae-sang
also come with you?

17:16.994 --> 17:18.829
I have nothing to do with them,
so let me go.

17:19.747 --> 17:20.748
You rebel.

17:23.751 --> 17:25.419
[whispers] Did I get that right?

17:26.003 --> 17:27.004
[Jun-taek scoffs]

17:28.756 --> 17:30.716
Please don't tell my father
I'm a rebel, won't you?

17:37.139 --> 17:38.599
You watch your mouth.

17:39.433 --> 17:41.435
How dare you talk to me that way?

17:42.061 --> 17:44.104
I don't care who your father is.

17:44.188 --> 17:47.691
Just know if you were to die
in this hospital, no one here will care.

17:49.234 --> 17:50.235
Is that clear?

17:55.657 --> 17:57.910
- Take him to the laboratory.
- [soldiers] Sir!

17:59.453 --> 18:00.496
[Jun-taek grunts]

18:06.835 --> 18:09.713
We can use this as leverage
to bribe his father for funding.

18:09.797 --> 18:10.923
Perfect timing.

18:11.590 --> 18:14.927
I want you to teach him a lesson,
but he stays alive.

18:17.304 --> 18:19.181
- [keys jangling]
- [door lock clicking]

18:19.264 --> 18:20.432
[soldier] Get in there!

18:21.350 --> 18:22.643
[Jun-taek grunting]

18:23.435 --> 18:24.686
[door lock clicks]

18:26.563 --> 18:28.148
Open this door! Open it!

18:28.816 --> 18:29.775
Open the door!

18:29.858 --> 18:31.026
[Jun-taek grunting]

18:31.110 --> 18:33.070
Let go! Let go!

18:33.153 --> 18:34.571
- [soldier] Stay still!
- [grunts]

18:34.655 --> 18:36.657
[breathing heavily]

18:38.117 --> 18:40.577
[Jun-taek groaning]

18:51.588 --> 18:53.590
[unsettling music playing]

18:56.135 --> 18:57.386
[exhales]

19:14.611 --> 19:15.445
[soldier 1] Sir!

19:17.364 --> 19:18.198
What is it?

19:18.282 --> 19:19.950
The platoon in disease control has found

19:20.701 --> 19:22.744
two intruders
in the second-level basement.

19:22.828 --> 19:24.663
They're being taken to Lt. Kato.

19:27.207 --> 19:29.209
[unsettling music playing]

19:38.677 --> 19:39.511
Who are they?

19:39.595 --> 19:41.597
Intruders who snuck
into the hospital, sir.

19:56.028 --> 19:57.112
[woman 1] It is Master Jang.

19:57.196 --> 19:59.907
- [man 1] Master Jang? Really?
- [woman 2] It is Master Jang.

19:59.990 --> 20:01.992
[prisoners chattering]

20:02.075 --> 20:03.118
Quiet!

20:03.202 --> 20:04.786
[chattering stops]

20:10.459 --> 20:12.377
I'll take this one here.

20:13.420 --> 20:15.339
- Just bring him.
- [soldier 2] Yes, sir.

20:15.422 --> 20:17.341
- [unsettling music playing]
- Wait! Where we going?

20:18.050 --> 20:20.135
- What about her?
- [soldier 1] She's staying here!

20:22.221 --> 20:23.680
Get your hands off her!

20:25.182 --> 20:26.225
What's this?

20:27.017 --> 20:28.393
So this is your woman.

20:29.102 --> 20:30.187
[soldier 2] Let's go.

20:30.270 --> 20:33.023
Stay where you are!
I promise I'll come back for you!

20:34.274 --> 20:35.651
You're mine now!

20:36.526 --> 20:40.113
Stay where you are. I'll find you!
I promise you! I'll come back for you!

20:51.917 --> 20:53.919
[breathing heavily]

21:02.386 --> 21:03.512
[low growling]

21:11.853 --> 21:13.105
[pen scratching]

21:13.188 --> 21:16.775
[Kato] The creature
may be more intelligent than expected.

21:18.652 --> 21:21.238
It learned how to use the elevator
on its own.

21:26.368 --> 21:29.663
It's now been more than an hour
since we lost sight of it.

21:31.748 --> 21:32.916
[ominous music playing]

21:38.046 --> 21:40.424
I wonder what it is that it's after.

21:45.804 --> 21:47.806
- [knocking at door]
- [door opens]

21:51.393 --> 21:54.062
[soldier] We've just captured
the intruders, Lieutenant.

21:54.146 --> 21:56.565
Apparently, they say
that they've seen the creature.

22:03.905 --> 22:04.948
[groans]

22:06.658 --> 22:08.660
- [tense music playing]
- [grunts]

22:24.551 --> 22:26.970
[breathing heavily]

22:47.240 --> 22:50.160
Now, you and I can finally talk.

22:52.162 --> 22:54.414
So why did you sneak into this building?

22:54.498 --> 22:56.416
What were you trying to do?

22:58.168 --> 22:59.753
There's someone I'm looking for here.

23:01.880 --> 23:04.341
You knew it was illegal
for you to be in here.

23:04.841 --> 23:06.843
Yet you trespassed anyways. Why?

23:06.927 --> 23:08.387
[chuckles]

23:10.097 --> 23:13.392
Okay, so it's illegal for me
to be inside of this hospital right now,

23:15.268 --> 23:17.771
yet somehow you can all
conduct human experiments in here?

23:22.442 --> 23:24.486
Show me

23:25.112 --> 23:26.196
some

23:27.072 --> 23:27.906
respect.

23:28.573 --> 23:32.285
How about you show me some respect first
instead of kicking and pushing me?

23:34.621 --> 23:36.373
Why are you so desperate for my attention?

23:38.834 --> 23:39.960
[Chae-ok grunts, groans]

23:46.299 --> 23:49.511
Now, why don't we start
from the very beginning?

23:49.594 --> 23:51.430
Why did you
break into this building tonight?

23:51.513 --> 23:52.806
And tell me the truth!

23:53.765 --> 23:55.767
[breathing heavily]

23:57.227 --> 23:58.895
[Tae-sang] What do you want with me?

23:59.771 --> 24:03.191
The Tokyo bombings recently.
You've heard, yes?

24:04.276 --> 24:07.404
A little,
but what's that got to do with this?

24:07.487 --> 24:10.365
I do not intend to return home.

24:11.283 --> 24:12.826
Even when the war is over.

24:13.577 --> 24:14.953
My family likes it here.

24:15.495 --> 24:18.623
It's nice here in Gyeongseong,
and they don't wanna go back either.

24:19.416 --> 24:20.459
Okay, so?

24:23.503 --> 24:26.548
You'll give me a lump sum of money
and a nice home.

24:28.592 --> 24:30.302
I want to open a new store as well.

24:31.595 --> 24:34.264
Provide me with these,
and you'll leave Ongseong Hospital alive.

24:34.347 --> 24:35.223
That's my offer.

24:39.102 --> 24:40.479
[Tae-sang exhales]

24:41.855 --> 24:44.608
And what makes you think
that I'll agree to any of this?

24:45.192 --> 24:48.528
You owe me one.
You're alive because I helped you earlier.

24:50.071 --> 24:52.741
Can we take a little peek
inside your cart, then?

25:01.750 --> 25:03.752
[mysterious music playing]

25:05.295 --> 25:07.631
[Sachimoto] Would you like
to check any other places?

25:07.714 --> 25:10.509
[Soma] No.
Enjoy your evening, Mr. Sachimoto.

25:12.636 --> 25:14.346
[Soma] To be honest, I was surprised.

25:15.096 --> 25:17.015
Though I knew you were here for Akiko,

25:18.141 --> 25:20.435
I didn't expect you
to help the kids as well.

25:22.562 --> 25:24.773
We call her Myeong-ja. Where is she?

25:27.067 --> 25:28.109
Just give up.

25:29.528 --> 25:31.905
There's no way you'll be able to free her.

25:32.989 --> 25:35.033
So just let it go and leave without her.

25:36.576 --> 25:39.996
Down inside of the prison,
you had a lot of Joseon people locked up.

25:41.164 --> 25:42.374
What are you all planning to do

25:42.457 --> 25:44.501
with all the innocent women and children
down there?

25:46.753 --> 25:49.172
And what about the horrible monster, huh?

25:50.507 --> 25:52.342
What's the point
of even making that thing?

25:52.968 --> 25:54.594
Are they running biological experiments?

25:54.678 --> 25:57.347
Is that what all the prisoners are for,
to be experimented on?

25:58.682 --> 25:59.641
[sighs]

26:00.350 --> 26:01.726
Does this mean that

26:03.228 --> 26:04.980
you're going to reject my offer?

26:05.480 --> 26:06.356
[sighs]

26:12.112 --> 26:13.238
Where's Chae-ok?

26:14.406 --> 26:16.741
The woman captured alongside me,
where is she?

26:17.534 --> 26:19.119
[groaning]

26:19.911 --> 26:21.913
[groaning]

26:23.373 --> 26:25.083
[groans, coughs]

26:25.166 --> 26:27.043
- That looked like it hurt.
- [all laugh]

26:27.127 --> 26:30.046
- She's taking a beating.
- [soldier 3] He really got her. Ooh!

26:30.797 --> 26:32.632
[grunts, coughs]

26:32.716 --> 26:34.801
[groans, coughs]

26:34.884 --> 26:36.761
[groans]

26:39.681 --> 26:42.142
[groaning]

26:42.225 --> 26:43.893
If you really wanna get out of here alive,

26:43.977 --> 26:46.187
then you'll accept my offer
and save yourself, huh?

26:46.271 --> 26:49.107
Well, if I leave here without Myeong-ja,
I'm dead anyhow.

26:50.984 --> 26:53.945
So why don't you just tell me
where both the women are, huh?

26:56.323 --> 26:57.699
Otherwise, it's no deal for me.

26:58.575 --> 26:59.576
[sighs]

27:00.285 --> 27:02.037
[groaning]

27:07.208 --> 27:11.004
Why did you break into this building?
Tell me what your plans were.

27:13.882 --> 27:15.592
Answer me right now!

27:19.971 --> 27:21.431
Go drop dead, okay?

27:22.265 --> 27:23.433
[scoffs]

27:26.561 --> 27:27.395
Come grab her.

27:40.325 --> 27:41.534
[Chae-ok breathing heavily]

28:03.223 --> 28:05.684
I'm very aware of how

28:06.393 --> 28:10.689
to deal with defiant women
such as yourself.

28:18.279 --> 28:19.572
Answer me, Josenjing!

28:19.656 --> 28:20.907
[buttons clattering]

28:26.079 --> 28:28.915
You may be able to violate me by force…

28:31.710 --> 28:34.212
but that doesn't give you
any power at all.

28:37.173 --> 28:38.508
You still don't know that yet?

28:38.591 --> 28:39.718
You little bitch.

28:39.801 --> 28:41.261
I'll kill you! [screams]

28:41.344 --> 28:42.929
- [door bursts open]
- [Kato] That's enough!

28:52.147 --> 28:54.107
That's enough for now, Sergeant Haneda.

28:54.190 --> 28:57.026
Lieutenant, I need to teach her a lesson.
She's defiant.

28:58.278 --> 28:59.821
Is it not obvious to you?

29:00.780 --> 29:02.198
She's not intimidated by you.

29:14.210 --> 29:16.629
[breathing shakily]

29:27.807 --> 29:29.309
[door lock clicks]

29:44.657 --> 29:46.201
- [sighs]
- [distant door opens]

29:51.748 --> 29:53.958
- [door closes]
- [melancholy music playing]

30:01.883 --> 30:03.134
[Mrs. Nawol] You were right.

30:04.469 --> 30:06.054
Just when you think

30:07.138 --> 30:09.808
the cherry blossoms
have bloomed splendidly,

30:10.809 --> 30:12.811
they've already begun to fall.

30:25.782 --> 30:28.284
[door opens, closes]

30:28.868 --> 30:30.995
- [footsteps approaching]
- [Mr. Gu] Mrs. Nawol.

30:32.038 --> 30:34.582
Have you heard from Master Jang at all?
He hasn't returned?

30:43.550 --> 30:45.134
So he still isn't back yet?

30:53.685 --> 30:57.355
You must not have
gotten any rest last night, Ishikawa.

30:57.438 --> 30:58.690
You were restless.

31:00.942 --> 31:01.818
Well,

31:03.319 --> 31:07.073
it looks like
I wasn't the only person out late, was I?

31:08.324 --> 31:09.242
That's right.

31:39.981 --> 31:40.857
Have a seat, sir.

31:44.485 --> 31:47.280
I got your message,
and I came here right away.

31:47.864 --> 31:50.325
So, uh, please tell me what's going on.

31:52.118 --> 31:54.954
- Do you want anything to drink?
- Some water would be great.

32:00.668 --> 32:02.629
I wanted to speak to you about your son.

32:02.712 --> 32:05.548
Unfortunately,
he's gotten himself in trouble.

32:05.632 --> 32:09.761
Last night, he was caught trespassing
inside Ongseong Hospital.

32:11.596 --> 32:15.516
This is just so embarrassing.
I'm sorry. I'm ashamed he did this.

32:15.600 --> 32:17.393
I'd say that's quite the understatement.

32:20.897 --> 32:22.857
This situation is very serious.

32:24.692 --> 32:27.737
It's more than just breaking and entering.

32:29.530 --> 32:31.532
I hear he's a rebel, too, so I'm told.

32:34.744 --> 32:36.996
If your son is convicted of a crime,

32:37.497 --> 32:40.166
your family and your company
would be in great danger.

32:40.249 --> 32:42.251
[unsettling music playing]

32:43.044 --> 32:44.087
[sighs]

32:49.801 --> 32:50.802
[moans]

33:01.020 --> 33:02.271
So you're a rebel?

33:04.107 --> 33:06.734
What is it… that you want?

33:08.152 --> 33:09.821
Is it Joseon's independence?

33:10.989 --> 33:12.615
It's something like that, right?

33:19.831 --> 33:22.208
[Jun-taek grunting]

33:24.919 --> 33:26.921
[groaning]

33:27.922 --> 33:28.840
[groans]

33:30.216 --> 33:31.509
[groans]

33:42.562 --> 33:43.938
To be honest,

33:45.106 --> 33:47.025
torture usually isn't my first choice.

33:50.486 --> 33:54.157
I find it exhausting, super messy,
and unpleasant to deal with.

33:55.199 --> 33:56.743
Instead, I would much prefer

33:57.618 --> 34:00.038
to put you in one of the jars
along with everyone else.

34:00.121 --> 34:02.582
Crack your head, slice your stomach…
It's simpler.

34:17.138 --> 34:19.432
I want you to write down
the names of your fellow intruders

34:19.515 --> 34:22.894
and the purpose of your intrusion,
along with who you were looking for.

34:24.979 --> 34:26.147
You have one hour.

34:26.939 --> 34:30.193
If you don't write down the names,
you'll stay locked in here.

34:31.069 --> 34:34.447
But after, we put you
on the dissection table for a little fun.

34:36.824 --> 34:38.826
[officer breathes deeply]

34:42.413 --> 34:45.041
Fighting for a free
and independent Joseon.

34:46.167 --> 34:48.086
You dream big.
I'll definitely give you that.

34:48.795 --> 34:52.131
You must be aware your father's company
depends on Director Ichiro.

34:52.215 --> 34:53.674
[chuckles]

34:53.758 --> 34:55.593
You're such an idiot, aren't you?

35:04.936 --> 35:06.938
[groans, sighs]

35:09.941 --> 35:11.734
[janitor] If you are able
to get down there,

35:11.818 --> 35:14.153
can you look for my little brother
as well?

35:14.737 --> 35:16.364
His name is Oh Sang-deok.

35:17.198 --> 35:19.283
He has a black birthmark
over his right ear.

35:19.367 --> 35:21.244
It's about the size of a small thumb.

35:26.082 --> 35:28.084
[retches, coughs]

35:28.709 --> 35:30.336
[coughs]

35:36.717 --> 35:37.760
[moans]

35:39.262 --> 35:40.138
[groans]

35:40.221 --> 35:42.306
Why do you do that to yourself, Jun-taek?

35:45.893 --> 35:46.936
[Jun-taek moans]

35:49.021 --> 35:51.732
Whatever your problems,
drinking's not the answer.

35:52.900 --> 35:53.943
[Jun-taek moans]

35:55.361 --> 35:56.362
[Jun-taek moans]

35:57.321 --> 35:59.907
Yeah, but I feel better
after throwing up, at least.

36:01.492 --> 36:03.995
Your family's called for you
several times already.

36:06.956 --> 36:08.833
I think maybe it's best you go home.

36:12.044 --> 36:13.087
Hey, Tae-sang.

36:16.924 --> 36:19.302
I'm ashamed
of my father's business dealings.

36:21.929 --> 36:25.224
My father has gotten so wealthy
out of betraying his own country.

36:25.308 --> 36:26.475
Can you believe that?

36:27.935 --> 36:30.062
I hate myself for living lavishly.

36:30.563 --> 36:32.481
At the same time, I'm very fortunate.

36:34.025 --> 36:37.570
The very same people who kiss up
to my father for money are

36:38.696 --> 36:41.949
the same people who always condemn us
when we turn our backs.

36:43.534 --> 36:45.745
They don't know what we do
behind the scenes.

36:48.122 --> 36:50.666
And that's why I beat up anybody
who tries to, um,

36:50.750 --> 36:52.835
point fingers at you or your family.

36:52.919 --> 36:54.337
[Jun-taek laughs]

36:56.047 --> 36:58.299
You are something else, did you know that?

36:59.342 --> 37:02.470
You threw the best punches back then
but never led a rebellion.

37:03.596 --> 37:06.933
I've always been more focused
on earning a good living, that's why.

37:08.726 --> 37:12.188
You're very intelligent.
And you're extremely competent.

37:14.273 --> 37:16.150
So why a pawnshop, of all things?

37:16.234 --> 37:17.401
[inhales deeply]

37:17.485 --> 37:20.363
Well, considering my charm and talents,

37:21.113 --> 37:22.615
it suits me quite well, you know?

37:24.825 --> 37:25.910
You don't ever…

37:27.119 --> 37:30.122
you don't ever dream of something bigger
for yourself, Tae-sang?

37:30.873 --> 37:33.042
You've always been the dreamer type.

37:33.125 --> 37:35.044
You've been asking me that
for the past ten years.

37:35.127 --> 37:36.295
Aren't you tired of it?

37:39.465 --> 37:41.092
You're such a good man inside.

37:43.135 --> 37:47.431
You're the only friend I have
who recognizes my sincerity and

37:49.016 --> 37:51.352
my patriotism, my everything, hmm?

37:54.230 --> 37:57.275
So come on! Join us
at the Patriotic Society, Tae-sang, huh?

37:57.358 --> 37:59.110
[laughing]

37:59.193 --> 38:02.363
Let go, Jun-taek. I don't want
my brand-new suit smelling of alcohol.

38:02.446 --> 38:05.366
Ah! Let's live fast and die young
for our own country!

38:05.449 --> 38:06.826
What do you say, huh?

38:08.536 --> 38:10.162
- [grunts]
- I don't want to, okay?

38:10.871 --> 38:13.708
I wanna live a really long life
without you in it.

38:13.791 --> 38:16.502
Hey! Wait! Wait! Whoa! Hey, wait!

38:16.585 --> 38:19.588
Wait, Tae-sang!
I'm not done yet. I'm not done, huh?

38:27.263 --> 38:28.139
[sighs]

38:34.895 --> 38:38.733
I guess even the filthy rich master
of the House of Golden Treasure

38:38.816 --> 38:40.276
can't escape prison either.

38:40.818 --> 38:45.031
You didn't think to bribe anyone Japanese
before you broke into the hospital?

38:45.698 --> 38:48.200
How did someone like you
end up here in the first place?

38:48.284 --> 38:49.869
[inhales] I'm curious myself.

38:50.453 --> 38:52.413
I'm here because of this Myeong-ja woman.

38:52.913 --> 38:53.831
Wait, hold on.

38:54.498 --> 38:57.293
Maybe I'm here
because of Commissioner Ishikawa?

38:57.835 --> 38:58.794
No, wait.

38:59.628 --> 39:01.547
Or maybe it's all because of his wife.

39:03.007 --> 39:03.841
So, um…

39:03.924 --> 39:05.217
[clears throat, sighs]

39:06.469 --> 39:07.845
…did you come in with Comrade Kwon?

39:08.763 --> 39:10.056
Just so you know,

39:10.139 --> 39:13.017
I don't deserve to be mentioned
in the same sentence as him.

39:13.517 --> 39:15.269
My friend has a noble purpose.

39:15.353 --> 39:18.481
He's risking his life for a noble cause
while I'm just saving one girl.

39:22.151 --> 39:25.571
And though, in the grand scheme of things,
human lives seem a bit trivial,

39:26.072 --> 39:28.741
for some unknown reason,
I'm quite terrified of losing my life.

39:32.995 --> 39:33.954
[sighs]

39:34.455 --> 39:36.957
Oh no. I talked too long, didn't I?

39:38.042 --> 39:41.921
I should probably stop rambling
and get ready to get on out of here.

39:43.506 --> 39:44.757
[man] What do you mean?

39:45.841 --> 39:47.301
Just how are you getting out of here?

39:48.886 --> 39:49.804
[chuckles softly]

39:50.346 --> 39:51.597
I'm Jang Tae-sang.

39:52.181 --> 39:55.267
You think someone as rich and influential
in Gyeongseong as me

39:55.351 --> 39:57.603
came in here
without knowing someone on the inside?

39:59.730 --> 40:00.731
[intriguing music playing]

40:00.815 --> 40:04.110
These are my terms. You'll grant me
the following three things.

40:05.903 --> 40:09.073
You will first call Mrs. Nawol
over at the House of Golden Treasure.

40:09.156 --> 40:10.866
[phone ringing]

40:18.124 --> 40:19.083
Master Jang?

40:20.000 --> 40:20.835
Yes.

40:21.460 --> 40:22.920
This is her speaking, yes.

40:23.003 --> 40:26.549
Master Jang has a message for you.
You'll need to write this down.

40:29.009 --> 40:30.094
I'm ready. Go ahead.

40:31.679 --> 40:33.264
What is your second request?

40:33.347 --> 40:36.767
Remove all your patrol men and soldiers
away from the prison cells.

40:36.851 --> 40:39.019
Both of you, I need you to come with me.

40:39.854 --> 40:40.813
Right now, sir?

40:42.815 --> 40:45.818
[Soma] It's about the specimen
located in the fourth-level basement.

40:45.901 --> 40:47.945
So shut up and follow my orders!

40:49.196 --> 40:50.114
Yes, sir.

40:52.783 --> 40:53.617
Hey!

40:54.118 --> 40:56.328
You over there! You come too!

40:56.412 --> 40:57.705
[soldier] Yes, sir!

40:57.788 --> 40:59.290
[door opens]

41:00.082 --> 41:00.916
[door closes]

41:10.050 --> 41:11.135
[key jangles]

41:17.683 --> 41:19.685
[music intensifies]

41:21.729 --> 41:24.607
Whoa, whoa! Wait, wait, wait!
Let us come with you, Master Jang!

41:24.690 --> 41:27.318
- Take us with you, huh?
- [man 2] Mr. Jang, don't abandon us!

41:27.401 --> 41:30.905
- Please take us too.
- [man 3] Help us, Master Jang! Help us!

41:30.988 --> 41:33.032
[all clamoring]

41:35.826 --> 41:37.495
Wait, wait. Master Jang.

41:37.578 --> 41:40.831
Just wait about half an hour or so.
I'll be back for you all then.

41:40.915 --> 41:43.125
How do you expect us to believe you, huh?

41:43.209 --> 41:45.044
What if you never come back?

41:45.711 --> 41:47.880
You're full of suspicions,
aren't you, Comrade Lee?

41:51.050 --> 41:53.427
I promise to come back, all right?

41:53.928 --> 41:56.847
So just wait here
until I come back for you all. Don't move.

41:57.348 --> 41:58.641
Okay.

41:59.934 --> 42:02.853
- Master Jang, be careful.
- [man 4] Wait, wait, Master Jang!

42:04.730 --> 42:08.984
I'm sorry, your third request is too much.
If you look for her, you might die.

42:09.068 --> 42:11.570
I will decide for myself
whether I do or do not die tonight.

42:13.739 --> 42:14.823
Yoon Chae-ok.

42:15.824 --> 42:17.493
Where is she being held, hmm?

42:19.411 --> 42:20.704
[music fades]

42:23.249 --> 42:24.208
Change into this.

42:43.727 --> 42:44.728
Thank you for the shirt.

42:48.941 --> 42:51.110
I haven't been in Gyeongseong very long.

42:52.361 --> 42:53.988
I was in Manchuria before this.

42:54.905 --> 42:56.949
Did you work in disease control then?

42:58.450 --> 43:00.911
Did you bring that creature
all the way from Manchuria?

43:03.622 --> 43:04.456
Who are you?

43:08.252 --> 43:09.461
Are you with the Resistance?

43:09.545 --> 43:13.048
My mother went missing ten years ago,
and I've been looking for her ever since.

43:14.842 --> 43:17.011
While searching for my mother, I saw

43:18.095 --> 43:20.639
what experiments you did
to Joseon citizens on Manwol.

43:23.017 --> 43:23.934
[breathes deeply]

43:24.435 --> 43:28.105
I never imagined I'd hear about
Manwol Island in Gyeongseong.

43:28.188 --> 43:31.442
I wanna know why you brought that creature
all the way to Gyeongseong.

43:34.111 --> 43:37.239
You know, as a scientist,
I am always curious, you see?

43:38.198 --> 43:40.701
I develop an affection
towards what I create.

43:41.535 --> 43:42.536
But I don't

43:43.495 --> 43:45.080
expect you to understand this.

43:53.922 --> 43:55.507
[unsettling music playing]

43:56.050 --> 43:57.134
By any chance…

43:59.053 --> 44:01.347
have you and I ever met each other before?

44:04.350 --> 44:05.351
Your eyes

44:07.019 --> 44:08.937
look a bit familiar to me.

44:16.987 --> 44:18.238
What did you say

44:19.782 --> 44:22.201
was the name
of your long-lost mother again?

44:23.577 --> 44:25.120
Her Japanese name was…

44:28.082 --> 44:28.916
Seishin.

44:49.061 --> 44:50.187
Tell me who you are.

44:51.021 --> 44:51.980
Well, it's

44:53.190 --> 44:54.233
Choi Seong-sim.

45:00.114 --> 45:01.073
Or Seishin.

45:11.542 --> 45:12.459
But why?

45:13.711 --> 45:15.671
Why are you asking about my mother?

45:20.968 --> 45:22.553
You said you saw the creature.

45:22.636 --> 45:23.762
How was it up close?

45:25.806 --> 45:26.807
It was horrifying.

45:27.850 --> 45:31.603
Did you notice
or feel anything else with the creature?

45:31.687 --> 45:33.397
Did anything seem familiar to you?

45:34.148 --> 45:35.107
Why do you ask?

45:36.567 --> 45:38.610
I was too busy running for my life.

45:40.112 --> 45:42.364
So I didn't have time
to take a closer peek at it.

45:48.162 --> 45:48.996
[sighs]

45:49.580 --> 45:51.373
Now it's my turn to get some answers.

45:52.875 --> 45:54.877
Why did you ask me about Seishin?

45:55.961 --> 45:57.212
What do you know, huh?

45:58.964 --> 46:00.382
Have you seen my mother around here?

46:07.765 --> 46:09.725
You aggravated the sergeant earlier.

46:11.477 --> 46:13.562
What's the point
in making yourself suffer like that?

46:14.229 --> 46:16.565
It wouldn't have mattered
how I acted towards him.

46:18.525 --> 46:19.777
He'd still have done the same.

46:22.738 --> 46:23.822
You may be right.

46:55.896 --> 46:57.898
[unsettling music playing]

47:20.212 --> 47:22.005
- Take her away.
- [soldier] Yes, sir.

47:30.639 --> 47:33.517
Do not touch her again
until I give you permission.

47:35.435 --> 47:36.979
And if you disobey my orders,

47:37.896 --> 47:40.107
you will be demoted to regular infantry.

47:40.190 --> 47:42.401
- [music subsides]
- [Kato] Do I make myself clear?

47:43.193 --> 47:44.278
[Haneda] Yes, sir.

47:55.080 --> 47:56.123
[door lock clicks]

48:02.379 --> 48:05.007
I'm not finished with you.

48:05.841 --> 48:07.509
I will kill you one way or another.

48:09.428 --> 48:11.680
I would like to see you try
'cause you're just

48:13.265 --> 48:15.684
an inferior soldier boy.

48:16.268 --> 48:18.729
- [soldier 1] "Inferior soldier boy"?
- [solider 2] "Soldier boy"?

48:18.812 --> 48:19.688
[soldiers laugh]

48:19.771 --> 48:21.440
- Soldier boy.
- Soldier boy.

48:21.523 --> 48:22.649
[laughter stops]

48:22.733 --> 48:23.859
Shut your mouths.

48:25.152 --> 48:26.737
You got a death wish?

48:26.820 --> 48:27.821
Huh?

48:31.533 --> 48:33.660
Officer Asano is asking for you, sir.

48:42.586 --> 48:44.212
[tense music playing]

48:44.296 --> 48:47.341
- [man 1] Which way should we go?
- [man 2] Let's take a left…

48:47.424 --> 48:48.508
Dammit.

49:18.914 --> 49:20.123
[exhales]

49:21.124 --> 49:22.042
[sighs]

49:28.966 --> 49:32.135
My son may be immature,
but he's my only son.

49:32.219 --> 49:33.720
The only child I have left.

49:33.804 --> 49:35.931
So please just let my son go.

49:36.807 --> 49:40.185
Mr. Ichiro, I beg you.
I beg you forgive him, sir.

49:43.063 --> 49:44.731
Please have mercy, Mr. Ichiro.

49:46.024 --> 49:47.150
[sighs]

49:47.234 --> 49:49.069
You've put me in a tight position.

49:53.156 --> 49:54.616
Let's see how this unfolds.

50:02.290 --> 50:03.375
[sighs]

50:04.418 --> 50:06.003
Is it all in the briefcase?

50:06.712 --> 50:07.629
Yes, sir.

50:08.171 --> 50:10.382
I completed what you instructed me to.

50:10.465 --> 50:12.467
[pensive music playing]

50:16.388 --> 50:17.973
[Jun-taek's father] He's a fickle man.

50:18.056 --> 50:20.517
We'll need to prepare
alternative plans as well.

50:21.268 --> 50:22.185
Yes, sir.

50:23.186 --> 50:25.272
[Mrs. Nawol] Why don't you
leave that up to us?

50:32.654 --> 50:35.032
Are you with the House of Golden Treasure?

50:35.532 --> 50:36.450
[Mrs. Nawol] Indeed.

50:36.533 --> 50:38.910
We are also coming up
with a plan of our own.

50:39.494 --> 50:41.038
Let's work together, Master Kwon.

50:42.873 --> 50:43.999
[sighs]

50:47.502 --> 50:48.628
[music fades]

50:52.257 --> 50:53.341
[sighs]

50:54.051 --> 50:56.053
[ethereal music playing]

51:52.776 --> 51:54.402
[wistful music playing]

51:55.862 --> 51:57.864
[crying]

52:02.285 --> 52:03.495
[crying continues]

52:08.917 --> 52:15.841
I MISS YOU, CHAE-OK
MY DEAR DAUGHTER

52:31.189 --> 52:33.275
[Kato] Have you and I
ever met each other before?

52:33.358 --> 52:36.361
Your eyes look a bit familiar to me.

52:37.362 --> 52:41.408
What did you say was
the name of your long-lost mother again?

52:43.326 --> 52:46.371
[sobbing]

53:01.720 --> 53:02.762
[Seong-sim] I want

53:04.139 --> 53:04.973
to live.

53:10.395 --> 53:11.980
I want to live…

53:16.776 --> 53:18.653
so I can see you,

53:19.487 --> 53:20.530
my dear

53:21.740 --> 53:22.866
daughter.

53:29.831 --> 53:31.917
Chae-ok, where are you?

53:35.337 --> 53:37.339
[sobs]

53:44.721 --> 53:46.806
[sobs]

54:02.113 --> 54:03.448
[crying]

54:04.699 --> 54:05.659
[sobs] Oh, Mom.

54:09.120 --> 54:10.497
[music fades]

54:15.543 --> 54:16.670
[soldier 1] I'm starving.

54:17.754 --> 54:18.964
How much longer?

54:19.047 --> 54:20.799
We still have another hour left.

54:40.568 --> 54:42.237
- It's the real thing.
- What is it?

54:43.154 --> 54:44.114
Caramel?

54:44.614 --> 54:47.826
Why would someone throw something
so valuable on the ground, huh?

54:47.909 --> 54:49.286
Oh, there's another one.

54:50.578 --> 54:51.997
[door opens]

54:57.210 --> 54:59.212
[unsettling music playing]

55:04.884 --> 55:06.553
[Tae-sang] Chae-ok, are you okay?

55:06.636 --> 55:08.263
[keys jangling]

55:14.394 --> 55:17.188
What's wrong? Hey, what happened?
Did someone hurt you?

55:23.111 --> 55:26.531
- [soothing music playing]
- What's going on? What's wrong, Chae-ok?

55:28.992 --> 55:30.744
My mother was inside this cell.

55:31.828 --> 55:32.912
How do you know?

55:35.123 --> 55:37.751
I MISS YOU, CHAE-OK
MY DEAR DAUGHTER

55:37.834 --> 55:40.170
- [intriguing music playing]
- So she was definitely here.

55:40.962 --> 55:42.797
And I think she might still be here.

55:49.637 --> 55:52.432
I understand where you're coming from,
but we need to find a way out,

55:52.515 --> 55:53.641
or we're stuck here.

55:57.145 --> 55:59.773
Master Jang, this is where it ends.
I'm going on alone.

56:00.273 --> 56:01.733
So continue with your original plan.

56:01.816 --> 56:03.735
Chae-ok, the original plan
included you too.

56:03.818 --> 56:06.988
I'm not leaving knowing that she is
somewhere inside of this building.

56:08.323 --> 56:10.075
I'm going to find my mother.

56:12.243 --> 56:13.411
Just listen.

56:13.495 --> 56:16.206
This place is swarming with soldiers
on every single floor.

56:16.289 --> 56:18.333
They're heavily armed,
and they're looking for us.

56:18.416 --> 56:21.086
On top of that, there's a monster
somewhere in this hospital

56:21.169 --> 56:22.796
that is way too powerful to beat alone.

56:23.797 --> 56:27.342
So, instead, how about this?
We both should escape for the time being.

56:27.842 --> 56:31.012
Once we're out, we'll find another way
to get information about your mother.

56:31.721 --> 56:34.933
If you stay here, that monster could
end up injuring you or, worse, kill you.

56:35.016 --> 56:37.268
How are you gonna defend yourself
on your own?

56:37.352 --> 56:39.562
And should something bad happen
to you, I--

56:39.646 --> 56:41.648
[melancholy music playing]

56:48.947 --> 56:50.031
Thank you for everything.

56:54.911 --> 56:57.956
I'm sorry I couldn't stay with you
until the very end, Master Jang.

57:16.808 --> 57:17.976
Do you really have to go?

57:19.185 --> 57:20.478
It's been ten years.

57:23.731 --> 57:25.942
In that time, I have been
to every place you can think of,

57:26.025 --> 57:27.485
hoping to find my mother.

57:29.446 --> 57:31.573
Now, for once,
I finally know where she is.

57:34.492 --> 57:35.785
So I'm going to go get her.

57:43.251 --> 57:45.253
[wistful music playing]

57:50.383 --> 57:51.843
No matter what, just stay alive.

58:24.542 --> 58:26.419
[watch clicking]

58:28.880 --> 58:30.882
[ethereal music playing]

58:53.905 --> 58:56.241
[sobbing]

59:03.665 --> 59:06.292
[crying]

59:10.421 --> 59:11.506
[sniffles]

59:13.675 --> 59:14.842
[sobs]

59:17.262 --> 59:23.309
THE HOUSE OF GOLDEN TREASURE

59:29.357 --> 59:30.984
[sobs]

59:31.067 --> 59:38.032
HOUSE OF GOLDEN TREASURE
MASTER JANG TAE-SANG

59:40.743 --> 59:42.745
[dramatic music playing]

59:53.256 --> 59:57.093
SLEUTH YOON CHAE-OK

01:00:06.644 --> 01:00:09.272
SLEUTH YOON JUNG-WON

01:00:12.025 --> 01:00:14.402
TO FIND LEE IN-HYEOK
OF THE PATRIOTIC SOCIETY

01:00:26.998 --> 01:00:29.000
[music subsides]

01:00:37.800 --> 01:00:38.885
[breathing heavily]

01:00:38.968 --> 01:00:41.054
What's this? Where did everybody go?

01:00:42.430 --> 01:00:44.432
[gunshot echoing]

01:00:48.186 --> 01:00:49.896
[rifle cocks]

01:00:52.857 --> 01:00:54.317
[breathing nervously]

01:00:55.026 --> 01:00:56.069
You do know her.

01:00:57.779 --> 01:00:59.822
She was kept prisoner
in the cell you put me in.

01:01:00.406 --> 01:01:02.325
[dramatic music playing]

01:01:04.077 --> 01:01:05.453
You better tell me where she is.

01:01:13.419 --> 01:01:14.962
Answer me!

01:01:18.049 --> 01:01:19.884
I want you to take me to her right now.

01:01:23.763 --> 01:01:25.515
[snarling]

01:01:34.107 --> 01:01:35.525
[gunshot]

01:01:39.821 --> 01:01:40.947
[gunshot]

01:01:41.030 --> 01:01:42.615
[dramatic music continues]

01:02:29.620 --> 01:02:31.205
[music subsides]

01:02:48.973 --> 01:02:50.975
[soothing music playing]

01:04:20.731 --> 01:04:22.733
[music intensifies]

01:05:07.612 --> 01:05:09.530
[music fades]
